# Platform & Environment Concerns

## Target Platform: Linux Mint

### Required System Dependencies

```bash
# JUCE GUI dependencies
sudo apt install libx11-xcb-dev libxcb-util-dev libxcb-cursor-dev \
                 libxcb-xkb-dev libxkbcommon-dev libxkbcommon-x11-dev \
                 libfontconfig1-dev libcairo2-dev libgtkmm-3.0-dev

# Additional dependencies
sudo apt install libsqlite3-dev libxcb-keysyms1-dev

# Build tools
sudo apt install cmake ninja-build build-essential
```

### VST3 Installation Path

- User installation: `~/.vst3/`
- System installation: `/usr/lib/vst3/` (not recommended for development)

### DAW: REAPER

**Why REAPER:**
- Native Linux support
- Fast plugin scanning
- Excellent VST3 compatibility
- Free evaluation period
- Active Linux community

**Testing Workflow:**
1. Build plugin: `cmake --build build`
2. Plugin auto-installs to `~/.vst3/` (COPY_PLUGIN_AFTER_BUILD)
3. REAPER: Right-click track → Insert virtual instrument
4. Rescan plugins if needed: Options → Preferences → VST → Clear cache/re-scan

## JUCE Framework (8.0.x)

### FetchContent Configuration

```cmake
include(FetchContent)
FetchContent_Declare(JUCE
    GIT_REPOSITORY https://github.com/juce-framework/JUCE.git
    GIT_TAG juce-8.0.4)

FetchContent_MakeAvailable(JUCE)
```

### Required JUCE Modules

| Module | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `juce_core` | Basic utilities, memory, threads |
| `juce_audio_basics` | Audio buffer, MIDI |
| `juce_audio_processors` | AudioProcessor base class |
| `juce_audio_plugin_client` | Plugin format glue code |
| `juce_gui_basics` | GUI components |
| `juce_gui_extra` | Additional GUI utilities |
| `juce_dsp` | DSP utilities (filters, oscillators) |

### Module Dependencies

```cmake
target_link_libraries(${PROJECT_NAME}
    PRIVATE
        juce::juce_audio_processors
        juce::juce_audio_plugin_client
        juce::juce_core
        juce::juce_gui_basics
        juce::juce_gui_extra
        juce::juce_dsp
)
```

